# UST.G3AP Monotone Full-Source Rank-Squeeze Lemma

Date: 2026-08-11

Status: `CLOSED_EXACT_LINEAR_ALGEBRA_LEMMA_REQUIRES_NUMERICAL_PREMISES`

## Setting

Let

\[
M_{\rm all}:F^{92{,}979}\longrightarrow F^{39{,}726}
\]

be the selected target-Macaulay map over the fixed field
\(F=\mathbf F_{101^6}\). Let \(M_S\) be the restriction to any subset of its
source rows, with the target coordinates unchanged. Assume independently that
the selected ordinary-top quotient is nonzero:

\[
\dim_F\operatorname{coker}(M_{\rm all})\geq 1.
\]

## Lemma

If an exact nonzero \(39{,}725\)-minor occurs in \(M_S\), then

\[
\operatorname{rank}(M_{\rm all})=39{,}725,
\qquad
\dim_F\operatorname{coker}(M_{\rm all})=1.
\]

Moreover, if a normalized nonzero functional
\(\lambda:F^{39{,}726}\to F\) annihilates all 92,979 rows of
\(M_{\rm all}\), then \(\lambda\) spans the dual of that one-dimensional
cokernel and is the exact finite reduction functional.

## Proof

Every row of \(M_S\) is a row of \(M_{\rm all}\), so row-span inclusion gives

\[
\operatorname{rank}(M_S)\leq \operatorname{rank}(M_{\rm all}).
\]

A nonzero \(39{,}725\)-minor of \(M_S\) therefore implies

\[
39{,}725\leq\operatorname{rank}(M_{\rm all}).
\]

The independent nonzero quotient class gives

\[
\operatorname{rank}(M_{\rm all})
\leq 39{,}726-1
=39{,}725.
\]

The two inequalities force equality, and rank-nullity in the target gives a
one-dimensional cokernel. Its annihilator in the dual target is therefore
one-dimensional. Any normalized nonzero functional annihilating every full-map
row is consequently its unique normalized generator.

## Required Numerical Premises

This lemma does not assert that the premises have been computed. Numerical
adoption requires all of the following:

1. exact source inclusion of every row used by the subset minor;
2. a nonzero 39,725-minor with independent exact rank replay;
3. the independently certified selected ordinary-top lower bound;
4. exact provenance for all 92,979 full-map rows; and
5. independent replay of the emitted functional on every full-map row.

No process exit, partial export, probabilistic rank estimate, characteristic-zero
promotion, response rank or physical Hull-Strominger endpoint is supplied by
this lemma.
